# Telegram CRM — environment configuration
#
# 1. Copy this file to .env:    cp .env.example .env
#    (Windows PowerShell:      Copy-Item .env.example .env)
# 2. Fill in the two values below.
# 3. The .env file is gitignored. Never commit it.
#
# How to obtain TELEGRAM_API_ID and TELEGRAM_API_HASH:
#   - Visit https://my.telegram.org/apps
#   - Sign in with the Telegram account that will send messages
#   - Click "Create new application" (name + short description; both can be anything)
#   - Copy the numeric api_id and the 32-character api_hash into this file
#
# Do NOT store a Telegram session string in this file.
# Sessions are persisted in the SQLite database (table: telegram_sessions)
# after running the login CLI script:  npm run telegram:login
# See README.md → "Telegram login" for the full flow.

TELEGRAM_API_ID=
TELEGRAM_API_HASH=
